WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.480
For a separate worked example, assume a
fictional process owner has approved

2
00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:10.488
temperature indication at 20, 40 and 60 °C
with error no greater

3
00:00:10.608 --> 00:00:14.043
than ±0.5 °C.

4
00:00:14.163 --> 00:00:18.643
These are teaching assumptions, not
general GMP tolerances or

5
00:00:18.763 --> 00:00:20.405
real project approvals.

6
00:00:20.525 --> 00:00:24.643
Requirement R-03 concerns indication
accuracy.

7
00:00:24.763 --> 00:00:29.413
It does not establish product temperature
uniformity, mixing performance or

8
00:00:29.533 --> 00:00:32.264
an acceptable manufacturing process range.

9
00:00:32.884 --> 00:00:39.967
The supplier lists three component error
bounds of ±0.2 °C each: sensor,

10
00:00:40.087 --> 00:00:41.644
transmitter and display.

11
00:00:41.764 --> 00:00:45.752
If they can all act in the same direction,
the simple worst-case sum

12
00:00:45.872 --> 00:00:48.240
is 0.6 °C.

13
00:00:48.360 --> 00:00:51.688
That exceeds the worked requirement of
0.5.

14
00:00:51.808 --> 00:00:54.918
Calling each component accurate would miss
the chain.

15
00:00:55.038 --> 00:00:59.987
This conservative teaching calculation is
not a complete uncertainty budget

16
00:01:00.107 --> 00:01:03.776
or an automatic rejection of every
possible design.

17
00:01:04.396 --> 00:01:11.202
The row identifies R-03, the criterion,
sensor schedule S-07 revision B

18
00:01:11.322 --> 00:01:12.730
and the calculation.

19
00:01:12.850 --> 00:01:15.218
Its decision is not demonstrated.

20
00:01:15.338 --> 00:01:20.266
The action is to propose a justified
measurement-chain design or revise the

21
00:01:20.386 --> 00:01:25.122
requirement through authorized change, not
quietly relax the criterion.

22
00:01:25.242 --> 00:01:28.890
Installation checks must confirm the
selected components.

23
00:01:29.010 --> 00:01:32.871
Operational testing must challenge the
assembled chain under

24
00:01:32.991 --> 00:01:34.399
the approved method.

25
00:01:34.519 --> 00:01:38.508
DQ plans this evidence; it does not invent
its results.

26
00:01:39.128 --> 00:01:42.435
Suppose the supplier proposes lower-error
components.

27
00:01:42.555 --> 00:01:47.163
Review their applicable conditions and
recalculate the chain; do not close

28
00:01:47.283 --> 00:01:50.227
the row merely because a new datasheet
arrived.

29
00:01:50.347 --> 00:01:54.507
If the revised design supports the
requirement, record the rationale

30
00:01:54.627 --> 00:01:56.014
and reviewer decision.

31
00:01:56.134 --> 00:01:59.675
Keep the later installation and
operational checks in

32
00:01:59.795 --> 00:02:01.374
the verification plan.

33
00:02:01.494 --> 00:02:04.096
Distinguish design evidence adequate from

34
00:02:04.216 --> 00:02:06.435
installed performance demonstrated.

35
00:02:06.555 --> 00:02:10.523
The workbook contains a filled row and a
blank row for practice.
